        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 85-year-old female patient, admitted on 06/05/2024 due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD). On admission, clinical examination revealed increased dyspnoea, reduced oxygen saturation, and audible wheezing. Arterial blood gas analysis confirmed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Chest X-ray showed pulmonary hyperinflation without signs of pneumonia or cardiac decompensation. Blood tests showed elevated inflammatory markers. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy, resulting in satisfactory clinical improvement. Vital signs were monitored continuously throughout the stay. She was discharged on 07/05/2024 in a stable condition. Please continue inhaled maintenance therapy and ensure close outpatient follow-up. Pulmonary rehabilitation is recommended. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Treating Physician]</div>"
            },
